# Trivy ignore file — scoped exceptions only, each with its reason written here.
#
# This file exists so that one known, documented, upstream-unfixed finding does not either hide
# behind a blanket `ignore-unfixed` or hold the whole pipeline red. Anything NOT listed here
# still fails the build at CRITICAL/HIGH.

# CVE-2026-76642 — util-linux (bsdutils, libblkid1, liblastlog2-2): unprivileged mount-helper
#   exit-status check allows privilege escalation via X-mount.idmap / X-mount.owner hooks.
#   WHY IGNORED: the image is based on python:3.12-slim = Debian trixie. Debian's security
#   tracker marks trixie VULNERABLE with no fix (util-linux <no-dsa>, classified minor) and the
#   fix (2.42.4-1) exists only in forky/sid. Docker Hub publishes no forky variant of the
#   `python` image, so there is no patched base to move to. `apt-get upgrade` cannot clear it.
#   This is tracked in docs/implementation/HANDOFF.md and re-check it when trixie gets a DSA or
#   a forky-based Python image is published — then delete this entry.
CVE-2026-76642
